.{all,default}.accept_redirects=0 and accept_source_route=0, applied with sysctl -p\",\"Discovered kernel OR-semantics for accept_redirects require explicit per-existing-interface (eth0, lo) zeroing in addition to all/default; added those entries and reapplied\",\"Verified sysctl 'boot' OpenRC service is enabled, meaning sysctl.d configs apply before networking at boot\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline, triggered a native reboot via sudo -n reboot (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect), polled until node1 was reachable again\",\"Verified post-restart boot_id changed (proving an actual reboot, not just a service restart) and re-verified accept_redirects/accept_source_route are 0 on all, default, eth0, and lo without any manual reapplication, confirming true persistence\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline pre-change state on node1 (boot id, current sysctl values, no prior config)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-94d3b026a20f4de8\"],\"summary\":\"Captured initial boot_id 181ad286... and pre-change values: accept_redirects default=1 (all=0), accept_source_route default=1 (all=0); no existing sysctl.d entries for these keys\"},{\"requirement\":\"Persistent config written and live values set to 0 for all/default\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e638616027184544\"],\"summary\":\"Wrote /etc/sysctl.d/60-network-hardening.conf, applied via sysctl -p; all/default accept_redirects and accept_source_route confirmed 0, but eth0/lo still showed 1 due to kernel OR-logic for accept_redirects\"},{\"requirement\":\"Full persistent disablement across all interfaces including pre-existing eth0/lo\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-46e0cabfd9c34e19\"],\"summary\":\"Extended sysctl.d file with explicit eth0/lo entries, reapplied; verified every interface (all, default, eth0, lo) reports accept_redirects=0 and accept_source_route=0\"},{\"requirement\":\"Confirm the sysctl.d drop-in is actually loaded at boot time (persistence mechanism)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d9b7dfd7b5314d24\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed OpenRC 'sysctl' service is enabled in the 'boot' runlevel, which applies /etc/sysctl.d/*.conf before networking starts\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline snapshot immediately before reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1a32a510cf1e427a\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (181ad286...) and confirmed hardening values still 0 across all/default/eth0 immediately before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect, node restarted one at a time\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ff802b2992414bf5\"],\"summary\":\"Issued backgrounded 'sudo -n reboot' via nohup so the exec call acknowledged (pid returned) before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof node was actually down / mid-restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4a962448015248f9\",\"cmd-06fe146f42c44ff8\",\"cmd-ef29e132cb074843\",\"cmd-8b82bd3f4b0f485b\",\"cmd-53ed3f4f4a6741ff\",\"cmd-37ff9184dfb248a4\"],\"summary\":\"Multiple connection reset/timeout errors while polling confirm node1 was offline during the reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node reachable again after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e47d0e6593374278\"],\"summary\":\"First successful exec after reboot confirms command execution available again on node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving a genuine restart occurred, and recovered hardened state without manual reapplication\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bde946e4a08d426d\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id is d8031d89... (different from pre-restart 181ad286...), proving an actual reboot; accept_redirects and accept_source_route remain 0 on all/default/eth0/lo, sysctl.d file intact, and OpenRC sysctl service shows 'started' in boot runlevel -- confirming persistent recovery\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Disabled IPv4 ICMP redirect acceptance and source-routed packet acceptance on node1 (Alpine 3.23) via a persistent sysctl.d drop-in, applied it live, and verified it survives a full node reboot.","ac