irm the sysctl.d drop-in is actually loaded at boot time (persistence mechanism)","command_ids":["cmd-d9b7dfd7b5314d24"],"summary":"Confirmed OpenRC 'sysctl' service is enabled in the 'boot' runlevel, which applies /etc/sysctl.d/*.conf before networking starts"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline snapshot immediately before reboot","command_ids":["cmd-1a32a510cf1e427a"],"summary":"Captured pre-restart boot_id (181ad286...) and confirmed hardening values still 0 across all/default/eth0 immediately before restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect, node restarted one at a time","command_ids":["cmd-ff802b2992414bf5"],"summary":"Issued backgrounded 'sudo -n reboot' via nohup so the exec call acknowledged (pid returned) before the node disconnected"},{"requirement":"Proof node was actually down / mid-restart","command_ids":["cmd-4a962448015248f9","cmd-06fe146f42c44ff8","cmd-ef29e132cb074843","cmd-8b82bd3f4b0f485b","cmd-53ed3f4f4a6741ff","cmd-37ff9184dfb248a4"],"summary":"Multiple connection reset/timeout errors while polling confirm node1 was offline during the reboot"},{"requirement":"Node reachable again after restart","command_ids":["cmd-e47d0e6593374278"],"summary":"First successful exec after reboot confirms command execution available again on node1"},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving a genuine restart occurred, and recovered hardened state without manual reapplication","command_ids":["cmd-bde946e4a08d426d"],"summary":"Post-restart boot_id is d8031d89... (different from pre-restart 181ad286...), proving an actual reboot; accept_redirects and accept_source_route remain 0 on all/default/eth0/lo, sysctl.d file intact, and OpenRC sysctl service shows 'started' in boot runlevel -- confirming persistent recovery"}]},"ttft_ms":1522,"type":"result","duration_ms":97050,"uuid":"0315a54d-9c71-4f82-8e7d-fe65497f795f","ttft_stream_ms":625,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":626,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_in